From: VipinVIP <VipinVIP@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: tzmem: do not enable the SHM bridge on sm6150

Once Linux enables the TrustZone SHM bridge on SM6150 (Snapdragon 675), TZ rejects every
PAS_INIT_IMAGE call (error 0xffcfffbb), so e.g. the Adreno zap shader can never be
authenticated.  Downstream never enables it.  Add qcom,sm6150 to the blacklist next to
sm7150/sm8150/sdm845.
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@
 	"qcom,sdm670", /* failure in GPU firmware loading */
 	"qcom,sdm845", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
 	"qcom,sm7150", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
+	"qcom,sm6150", /* PAS_INIT_IMAGE is rejected once Linux enables the SHM bridge */
 	"qcom,sm8150", /* reset in rmtfs memory assignment */
 	NULL
 };
